title: AWS Network Load Balancer
agents: aws
catalog: cloud/aws
license: WTFPL
distribution: check_mk
description:
 This check monitors AWS Network Load Balancer (NLB) metrics via CloudWatch.
 It provides visibility into load balancer performance at the network layer.

 Monitored metrics:

 - Active Flow Count: Number of concurrent TCP/UDP flows

 - New Flow Count: Number of new flows established

 - Processed Bytes: Total bytes processed

 - Healthy/Unhealthy Target Count: Number of healthy and unhealthy targets

 - TCP Reset Counts: Client, Target, and NLB initiated resets

 Shown in the service details only (no thresholds, graphed):
 Active flows, new flows and processed bytes per protocol
 (TCP/UDP/TLS), processed packets, consumed LCUs, client/target TLS errors.

 Thresholds can be configured for active flows, new flows, processed bytes,
 and unhealthy targets.

discovery:
 One service is created for each Network Load Balancer discovered.
